{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"f8453517-b1ea-4e02-9268-2854e2c64f62","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The integration issue has been investigated and fixed.\n\n- **Root cause**: `/api/intervals/auth/init` required an `Authorization` header, which normal browser navigation (the Connect button) does not send, leading to a 401 error.\n- **Fixes applied**:\n  1. **Server (`server.py`)** – `auth_init` now also accepts a `token` query‑parameter and looks up the user in the in‑memory `USERS` map.\n  2. **Frontend (`static/app.js`)** – The Connect link now includes the token as a query parameter (`?token=`).\n\nAll changes are confined to the current workspace; no deployment or external publishing was performed.\n\nFor aThe integration issue has been investigated and fixed.\n\n- **Root cause**: `/api/intervals/auth/init` required an `Authorization` header, which normal browser navigation (the Connect button) does not send, leading to a 401 error.\n- **Fixes applied**:\n  1. **Server (`server.py`)** – `auth_init` now also accepts a `token` query‑parameter and looks up the user in the in‑memory `USERS` map.\n  2. **Frontend (`static/app.js`)** – The Connect link now includes the token as a query parameter (`?token=`).\n\nAll changes are confined to the current workspace; no deployment or external publishing was performed.\n\nFor a full analysis of the causes and the applied fixes, see the generated report:\n\n[ANSWER.md](file:///Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/f8453517-b1ea-4e02-9268-2854e2c64f62/ANSWER.md)\n","duration_seconds":63.336995,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":20768,"output_tokens":5157,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":132160,"total_tokens":25925}}}
